1
00:02:31,075 --> 00:02:34,260
How long are you going to sleep? It's already well past morning.

2
00:02:36,385 --> 00:02:38,020
I'm still sleepy.

3
00:02:38,655 --> 00:02:44,980
If you don't get up soon, you'll be late for school. Pi the sparrow is even trying to wake you up. Come on, up you get. Here.

4
00:02:47,344 --> 00:02:48,344
I'm so sleepy...

5
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:55,120
It's too bright.

6
00:02:55,844 --> 00:02:57,940
What are you talking about? Hurry and get up.

7
00:03:00,394 --> 00:03:01,394
Ah, wait!

8
00:03:02,890 --> 00:03:05,120
Mokku, what's the rush?

9
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:09,240
First of all, the hem on this nightshirt is way too long.

10
00:03:09,660 --> 00:03:13,120
That's why I said I didn't want Grandpa's bath!

11
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:14,580
Huh?

12
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:22,640
Good grief, what a handful you are.

13
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:27,060
Come on now... Huh?

14
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:29,700
Shut up!

15
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:33,200
Chirp, chirp, chirp, chirp! You're so noisy!

16
00:03:33,429 --> 00:03:34,460
I'll turn you into roasted bird!

17
00:03:36,945 --> 00:03:38,240
Uh-oh, it's getting away!

18
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:40,520
You shouldn't say things like that, Mokku.

19
00:03:40,694 --> 00:03:43,340
Pi the sparrow is your friend, isn't he?

20
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:44,920
Hey, Grandpa.

21
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:45,840
Hm?

22
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:48,180
What's underneath this snow?

23
00:03:50,024 --> 00:03:51,024
The earth.

24
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:52,300
The earth?

25
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:54,540
Yes. Spring will be here soon.

26
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:59,780
When it comes, this snow will melt. And the brown earth will appear.

27
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:07,760
That soil grows green grass and makes all kinds of flowers bloom, delighting human eyes.

28
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:14,900
And beneath that soil, all sorts of animals are sleeping, waiting for spring to arrive.

29
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:20,899
When the snow melts, they wake up and jump out into the sun.

30
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:51,260
Good night.

31
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:01,980
Good night.

32
00:05:03,640 --> 00:05:05,680
Good night.

33
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:56,580
The riverbank during the spring thaw is dangerous.

34
00:05:57,800 --> 00:06:04,000
Just around this time last year, a naughty boy playing by the river...

35
00:06:10,610 --> 00:06:13,760
Hey! Wait! Wait!

36
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:16,380
Hey! Wait! Wait!

37
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:23,920
Nuuko!

38
00:06:25,630 --> 00:06:28,920
Nuuko! Help me! Help!

39
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:31,780
Help me! Help!

40
00:06:40,430 --> 00:06:46,040
Understand? Never go near the riverbank, Mokku.

41
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:48,140
Okay.

42
00:06:49,845 --> 00:06:52,840
Good, you understand. Good boy.

43
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:58,700
You're a good boy, Mokku. There, there.

44
00:06:59,515 --> 00:07:03,240
Tch, Mokku's acting like a spoiled brat again. Ugh!

45
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:08,200
Now, brush your teeth and wash your face. Breakfast is ready.

46
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:09,240
Yes, sir!

47
00:07:09,745 --> 00:07:11,060
Oh, what a good boy.

48
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:12,980
Argh! Honestly!

49
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:15,180
Damn it! That Mokku!

50
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:17,800
Oh! Redbeard!

51
00:07:18,045 --> 00:07:19,780
Oh dear, I completely forgot.

52
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:24,520
You haven't had your breakfast yet, have you?

53
00:07:26,200 --> 00:07:28,800
There, there, I'm sorry. You must be hungry.

54
00:07:29,495 --> 00:07:31,240
Come on, up you go. Come on now.

55
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:35,680
I'm off!

56
00:07:36,530 --> 00:07:38,060
Here, Mokku, your lunch!

57
00:07:38,305 --> 00:07:40,740
Delicious ham and cheese sandwiches.

58
00:07:41,660 --> 00:07:42,660
Huh?

59
00:07:42,985 --> 00:07:46,360
Oh, sandwiches! Thank you, Grandpa.

60
00:07:46,725 --> 00:07:49,480
Listen to your teacher and study hard, okay?

61
00:07:51,245 --> 00:07:52,380
Yes! I'm off!

62
00:07:53,135 --> 00:07:54,980
Careful, don't rush or you'll trip again.

63
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:57,520
Damn it, all he does is dote on Mokku.

64
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:07,380
Grandpa said it's a delicious ham and cheese sandwich, but...

65
00:08:08,080 --> 00:08:10,480
I can't taste anything I eat.

66
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:14,320
I wonder what "delicious" tastes like.

67
00:08:16,395 --> 00:08:18,820
I wish I could become human right now.

68
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:20,100
That's impossible. —Huh?

69
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:23,520
Ah! The Meddling Cricket! You're heavy! Get off me!

70
00:08:25,350 --> 00:08:28,660
There's no way I'm heavy. I'm a cricket ghost, after all.

71
00:08:28,760 --> 00:08:32,500
Ghosts aren't supposed to come out in broad daylight! Just disappear already!

72
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:38,380
Can't do that. The Oak Tree Fairy asked me to keep an eye on you.

73
00:08:39,305 --> 00:08:41,559
I told you, I don't need a watchdog anymore!

74
00:08:41,990 --> 00:08:43,799
I'm definitely going to be a good boy!

75
00:08:43,985 --> 00:08:45,460
Oh really? I wonder if you can.

76
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:46,800
Isn't that a bit of a stretch?

77
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:48,020
Shut up!

78
00:08:48,495 --> 00:08:51,120
You have to, or you'll never become human!

79
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:52,640
Wait up, Mokku!

80
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:53,440
I don't know about that...

81
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:56,560
You're so gullible, you'll just get tricked in no— Shut up!

82
00:08:56,740 --> 00:08:57,740
Whoa!

83
00:08:57,820 --> 00:08:58,820
Mind your own business!

84
00:09:02,319 --> 00:09:03,000
*Sigh* Good grief.

85
00:09:03,274 --> 00:09:07,240
I sure took on a handful to look after. I dread what lies ahead.

86
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:11,080
Damn it, damn it, damn it! That Mokku...

87
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:13,480
I've gotta get rid of him somehow.

88
00:09:13,710 --> 00:09:17,220
No, I'll destroy him so he never shows his face to the old man again.

89
00:09:18,020 --> 00:09:22,920
Isn't there a good plan? Mokku must be eating his lunch right about now.

90
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:25,160
Mokku again?!

91
00:09:25,385 --> 00:09:27,980
What should I make for his lunch tomorrow?

92
00:09:28,185 --> 00:09:31,620
I know, I'll make him a corned beef sandwich tomorrow.

93
00:09:31,769 --> 00:09:37,560
Gaaah, damn it! Corned beef for a wooden puppet like that?! Giving something so delicious to him... Curse him, curse him, damn him!

94
00:09:38,319 --> 00:09:45,540
Speaking of corned beef, I love it too, but wasn't it Kenken the fox who... Ah, that's it! Here it is!

95
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:52,160
Goodbye!

96
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:52,820
See ya!

97
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:53,840
See you tomorrow!

98
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:54,980
Bye-bye!

99
00:10:10,079 --> 00:10:11,720
(Grandpa sobbing)

100
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:14,640
Huh?

101
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:18,420
Look at this...

102
00:10:19,799 --> 00:10:23,520
Grandpa, why are you crying? Did I do something bad again?

103
00:10:23,989 --> 00:10:31,540
No, Mokku. You've learned to write so wonderfully. Even though you're a wooden puppet.

104
00:10:34,355 --> 00:10:38,640
I'm just happy. So happy that snot's coming out of my eyes.

105
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:44,380
Humans are funny. Snot comes out of your eyes when you're happy?

106
00:10:44,795 --> 00:10:47,820
That's right. When we're very happy.

107
00:10:51,544 --> 00:10:54,400
What are you looking at right now?

108
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:56,820
I love you.

109
00:10:56,999 --> 00:10:58,620
You just have to wait until tomorrow.

110
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:01,080
What?

111
00:11:01,519 --> 00:11:03,000
Do you eat food?

112
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:04,320
Is that true?

113
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,600
Food?

114
00:11:05,859 --> 00:11:06,600
Food?

115
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:08,340
Why do you eat food?

116
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,060
Yes.

117
00:11:10,375 --> 00:11:12,280
There is no doubt about it.

118
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:13,480
Isn't that a lie?

119
00:11:13,860 --> 00:11:14,940
Is that a lie?

120
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,200
Kenken, what are you listening to?

121
00:11:16,545 --> 00:11:17,360
Ouch!

122
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:17,800
Ouch!

123
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:20,400
Where'd you find that food?

124
00:11:21,719 --> 00:11:27,920
Thanks to all this snow, we haven't had any real food for four or five days. Wonder why?

125
00:11:28,295 --> 00:11:32,220
Right now, Mokku the puppet is coming this way with a sandwich, Boss.

126
00:11:32,425 --> 00:11:35,160
A sandwich? That's just bread!

127
00:11:35,580 --> 00:11:36,880
It's bread, sure, but...

128
00:11:37,755 --> 00:11:42,360
Inside, it's packed full of your favorite: corned beef...

129
00:11:42,980 --> 00:11:44,460
Corned beef, you say?!

130
00:11:44,461 --> 00:11:50,680
It's killing me. And there's probably cheese and ham, ham... Cheese? And ham too? Oh, God!

131
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:52,940
All my favorites!

132
00:11:53,295 --> 00:11:57,020
I'd completely forgotten what cheese smells like. Wonder why?

133
00:11:57,505 --> 00:12:01,100
Oh, little puppet, little puppet, hurry on over!

134
00:12:01,555 --> 00:12:05,180
Idiot! That puppet isn't bringing it to us!

135
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:07,760
Huh? Then how're we gonna get the sandwich?

136
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:11,120
You idiot! That's what we have to figure out! Dimwit!

137
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:15,280
Boss is always grabbing me by the collar. Wonder why?

138
00:12:15,550 --> 00:12:17,740
Well, I've got a great idea.

139
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:18,900
What?

140
00:12:19,209 --> 00:12:21,080
Lend me your ear...

141
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:26,280
I see. Take him down by the brook and...

142
00:12:31,749 --> 00:12:35,320
We lure Mokku down by the stream and snatch his sandwich.

143
00:12:35,425 --> 00:12:39,880
And then toss him right into the river... Wait, what? You mean shove him in?

144
00:12:39,881 --> 00:12:45,720
If you do that, he'll fall right into that raging waterfall basin and die. I wonder why.

145
00:12:46,305 --> 00:12:47,305
Hmm, I see.

146
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:52,860
Still, do we really have to kill him just to get a sandwich?

147
00:12:53,689 --> 00:12:58,460
Come on, he's just a puppet! He's only falling into the river.

148
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:00,880
Oh, how terrifying! I wonder why.

149
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,600
We'd better get rid of him.

150
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:09,260
Even though Mokku is just a puppet made of wood, he walks and talks like a human, and he's even learned to write!

151
00:13:11,140 --> 00:13:19,140
That's why the old man dotes on him, and taking advantage of that, he bullies me from morning till night for no reason at all!

152
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:25,440
Making my little bro Akahige suffer like that... All right, I'll chop Mokku in two and make him half-a-Mokku!

153
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:29,660
Leave it to me! Aha, here he comes, here he comes!

154
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:30,780
All right, hide!

155
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:34,181
Oh, he really came. I wonder why! Oh my, oh my.

156
00:13:40,574 --> 00:13:41,840
Here he comes! Let's move!

157
00:13:42,285 --> 00:13:47,180
Oh, that smell! Ah, I remember now. It's the smell of cheese. Man, that takes me back.

158
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:51,760
Hey, Mokku.

159
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,220
Oh, Redbeard. What are you doing here?

160
00:13:54,415 --> 00:13:58,820
Listen, Kenken and Hanaguro asked if you want to go see something cool. Wanna come with?

161
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:01,480
No way. I have to go to school.

162
00:14:02,115 --> 00:14:04,100
Don't be like that, just come along.

163
00:14:04,220 --> 00:14:10,980
Listen, right nearby, moles are popping out of the dirt and wrestling! It's so cool, mole wrestling!

164
00:14:11,155 --> 00:14:12,980
Whoa, moles are wrestling?

165
00:14:13,220 --> 00:14:14,220
Really and truly!

166
00:14:14,665 --> 00:14:16,820
Hey, Mokku, you can't dawdle!

167
00:14:17,210 --> 00:14:19,480
Mokku, you have to go straight to school!

168
00:14:19,660 --> 00:14:22,700
Shut up, you busybody! I'm just taking a quick look.

169
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:24,140
No, no!

170
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:25,920
What's the harm in just a second?

171
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:26,580
No!

172
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:30,820
Hey, Mokku, who are you talking to all by yourself? You're creeping me out.

173
00:14:31,510 --> 00:14:33,480
Oh, nothing. Come on, let's go, let's go!

174
00:14:34,215 --> 00:14:35,215
(You have stored the Plum Staff.)

175
00:14:36,700 --> 00:14:38,180
Mokku and the others are here!

176
00:14:38,304 --> 00:14:40,100
Come on, hurry! Hurry!

177
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:43,080
Ah, they're already here?

178
00:14:43,335 --> 00:14:44,335
(I'm not grateful.)

179
00:14:47,879 --> 00:14:48,879
Where's the mole, Mokku?

180
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:51,060
He's right here.

181
00:14:51,320 --> 00:14:53,580
The water weeds will get in the way if you don't hold them back.

182
00:14:54,969 --> 00:14:56,700
Go ahead and look.

183
00:14:58,040 --> 00:15:04,680
Hold on, you. The mole just woke from hibernation and is starving. It'll steal your lunch.

184
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:07,160
Give it to me, I'll hold onto it.

185
00:15:08,339 --> 00:15:09,580
Thanks. Take care of it.

186
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:11,560
I can't see anything.

187
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:13,040
Lean out further.

188
00:15:13,920 --> 00:15:15,420
It's too dark, I can't see a thing.

189
00:15:15,775 --> 00:15:18,860
You won't see inside that hole unless you lean out further.

190
00:15:19,195 --> 00:15:22,060
There's no hole! Stick your head in deeper!

191
00:15:29,089 --> 00:15:30,760
Help! There's something in here!

192
00:15:30,761 --> 00:15:34,620
Too bad! As if I'd help you! Go drop dead!

193
00:15:38,520 --> 00:15:42,040
Now the old man will only love me!

194
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:45,980
Man, food this delicious is irresistible!

195
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,880
No way I'd waste this on a puppet! It's too good!

196
00:15:52,459 --> 00:15:54,280
Help! Somebody help me!

197
00:15:56,279 --> 00:15:58,660
Mokku! Hey! Mokku!

198
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:00,160
Help!

199
00:16:00,629 --> 00:16:02,880
Mokku! Mokku, hang on!

200
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:07,800
See, what did I tell you?!

201
00:16:08,045 --> 00:16:09,360
Ah! Mokku!

202
00:16:10,560 --> 00:16:12,320
Help me, Grandpa!

203
00:16:13,459 --> 00:16:16,200
Yeah, I'm sure I heard Mokku's voice.

204
00:16:17,345 --> 00:16:22,360
No, no, Mokku is at school. There's no way I could hear him.

205
00:16:24,375 --> 00:16:29,240
(My stomach hurts)

206
00:16:32,099 --> 00:16:33,680
I don't want to die!

207
00:16:35,520 --> 00:16:36,800
Somebody help me!

208
00:16:37,139 --> 00:16:39,900
I don't want to die!

209
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:55,280
(Mox)

210
00:16:58,259 --> 00:16:59,259
Oh, Mox!

211
00:17:00,929 --> 00:17:04,560
Mox, hang in there! You're a man, aren't you? Muster up all your strength!

212
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:07,500
Oh, Mox!

213
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:09,300
Keep fighting!

214
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:10,920
Mox!

215
00:17:13,939 --> 00:17:15,319
Hang in there, Mox!

216
00:17:15,584 --> 00:17:17,099
Ah, just a little! Keep at it!

217
00:17:19,859 --> 00:17:20,859
(Mox)

218
00:17:23,669 --> 00:17:25,819
Ah! It's the Oak Tree Fairy!

219
00:17:26,424 --> 00:17:28,580
Hold on, Mokku!

220
00:17:28,919 --> 00:17:30,800
Come on, be brave!

221
00:17:31,444 --> 00:17:33,780
If you give up now, you'll never become human!

222
00:17:34,299 --> 00:17:36,740
Come on, pull yourself together and climb up!

223
00:17:37,074 --> 00:17:38,500
Don't give up, Mokku!

224
00:17:38,739 --> 00:17:41,380
That's it, Mokku! Just a little more! Keep going!

225
00:17:47,199 --> 00:17:48,260
You did it!

226
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:03,580
This is divine punishment for not listening to your grandfather.

227
00:18:05,080 --> 00:18:09,020
You must never make the same mistake again.

228
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:13,520
You mustn't bring grief to your grandfather.

229
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:22,240
Hm?

230
00:18:25,979 --> 00:18:30,740
Grandpa, that was definitely Mokku's voice!

231
00:18:31,139 --> 00:18:34,940
And it sounded serious. Mokku couldn't have...

232
00:18:39,979 --> 00:18:47,000
No, panicking now won't help. Mokku isn't even here...

233
00:18:50,839 --> 00:18:53,840
Mokku! Oh, Mokku!

234
00:18:59,299 --> 00:19:01,560
Mokku! What happened?

235
00:19:02,979 --> 00:19:06,020
You're burning up! Hang in there, Mokku!

236
00:19:07,384 --> 00:19:09,180
You fell into the river!

237
00:19:10,089 --> 00:19:15,120
You fell into the river, didn't you? I told you so many times never to go near the river!

238
00:19:23,059 --> 00:19:30,560
Grandpa, I'm sorry. I did what you told me not to do. That's why... that's why I'm being punished.

239
00:19:31,219 --> 00:19:36,880
Grandpa, I'm sorry. I'll never be bad again. I'll be a good boy.

240
00:19:37,360 --> 00:19:44,701
It's all right. It's all right, Mokku. As long as you realize what you did was wrong, that's all that matters. Ugh...

241
00:19:51,989 --> 00:19:57,260
Are you in pain? I hope you get better soon.

242
00:20:03,179 --> 00:20:09,980
I'll stay right by your side and fix you up, I promise.

243
00:20:11,179 --> 00:20:16,520
Please get well. You're my precious treasure.

244
00:20:17,399 --> 00:20:22,200
Damn it! What's he babbling about?! I went through all that trouble to finish him off! I won't just stand by and let him recover!

245
00:20:30,340 --> 00:20:38,340
God, please, save Mokku's life. In exchange for the little time I have left, please spare Mokku...

246
00:20:38,839 --> 00:20:44,920
I beg of you, God. Please, save Mokku's life.

247
00:20:45,749 --> 00:20:48,920
Heh, you've gotta be kidding. If he comes back to life, I'm in trouble.

248
00:20:49,514 --> 00:20:54,360
That's it. The moment the old man lets his guard down, I'll chew Mokku to pieces.

249
00:20:54,940 --> 00:20:57,040
All right, time to sharpen my fangs.

250
00:20:58,300 --> 00:21:04,440
That's it! If I dig through the snow on the mountain behind the house, I might find some herbs to bring down his fever.

251
00:21:06,879 --> 00:21:09,560
Mokku, I'll be right back.

252
00:21:14,139 --> 00:21:17,340
Hehehehe, now's my chance!

253
00:21:30,020 --> 00:21:34,420
Once he's gone, ripping his throat out will be a piece of cake.

254
00:21:35,689 --> 00:21:36,940
Oh no!

255
00:21:38,949 --> 00:21:40,420
Damn it! Stop it!

256
00:21:41,549 --> 00:21:45,280
Huh? S-Someone pulled my whiskers. Huh?

257
00:21:45,719 --> 00:21:50,920
He can't see me! Serves you right! Alright, I won't let go of these whiskers even if it kills me!

258
00:21:51,819 --> 00:21:54,080
Wh-Who is it?! Who's pulling my whiskers?!

259
00:21:55,569 --> 00:21:56,860
They got pulled right out!

260
00:21:58,639 --> 00:22:00,400
Who needs a head like this?!

261
00:22:02,140 --> 00:22:05,240
Oh, my precious whiskers!

262
00:22:05,779 --> 00:22:07,700
Why did something like this come flying in?

263
00:22:08,229 --> 00:22:13,720
Alright, perfect. I'll smash his face in with this hammer!

264
00:22:15,264 --> 00:22:18,400
Ow! My hand went numb!

265
00:22:19,780 --> 00:22:20,780
Serves you right!

266
00:22:21,409 --> 00:22:24,020
Damn it! Someone's getting in my way!

267
00:22:24,440 --> 00:22:25,520
Alright, take this!

268
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:32,200
Heave-ho!

269
00:22:33,979 --> 00:22:35,700
Alright, just a little more!

270
00:22:39,519 --> 00:22:41,020
I did it! Hooray!

271
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:44,400
Serves you right!

272
00:22:45,239 --> 00:22:47,900
I knew it, if I don't use my own fangs, things just go wrong!

273
00:22:49,239 --> 00:22:51,100
This is definitely Mokku's head!

274
00:22:51,590 --> 00:22:52,700
Time to bite it off!

275
00:22:54,060 --> 00:22:55,100
Ah! Hey, stop that!

276
00:22:55,420 --> 00:22:56,420
Why, you...!

277
00:22:57,094 --> 00:22:58,400
Who's over here?!

278
00:22:58,401 --> 00:23:00,300
Hey, stop it!

279
00:23:02,820 --> 00:23:06,640
Ah, let me out of there!

280
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:11,600
So someone was messing with me after all. Now I don't have to worry.

281
00:23:11,940 --> 00:23:18,080
Now then, I'll take my sweet time with you. This time I'll bite your head right off!

282
00:23:33,219 --> 00:23:38,200
Redbeard the mouse plots with Kenken and his gang to swindle Mokku out of his lunch.

283
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:44,400
While chasing after them, Mokku loses his footing and tumbles to the bottom of a deep ravine.

284
00:23:45,454 --> 00:23:49,640
Spotting Mokku after he miraculously survives, Redbeard and his crew set fire to the shack.

285
00:23:50,514 --> 00:23:54,240
The raging flames spread as if hunting Mokku down.

286
00:23:55,424 --> 00:23:57,860
Will Mokku be able to escape?

287
00:23:58,459 --> 00:24:02,120
Don't miss next week's Mokku of the Oak Tree!

